# Activatable-states registry (P1c) — DATA enumeration of states SFS can both
# DETECT and SAFELY APPLY. Backs policies/zero-knowledge-activation.md.
#
# Format (pipe-delimited):  <state-id>|<offer-path-test>|<description>
#   - lines starting with '#' and blank lines are ignored.
#   - <offer-path-test> is a tests/test-*.sh file that proves the
#     detect -> guide -> consent(once) -> apply path for the state.
#
# Contract enforced by tests/test-activatable-states-registry.sh:
#   every registered state MUST own an existing offer-path test, or run-all
#   FAILS. A new activatable state added here without an offer-path test cannot
#   pass — that is the point. States needing genuine human judgement
#   (architecture/provider choice, irreversible/outward actions) are NOT
#   activatable states and must not be listed; they stay explicit user choices.
team-topology-activation|test-team-auto-offer.sh|solo -> trio multi-agent activation: detect capable runtimes (lead+worker) -> R5 one-line [Y/n] offer on upgrade -> apply preset on consent; decline remembered, standalone solo lock.
deprecated-fallback-promotion|test-team-fallback-promotion.sh|deprecated gemini fallback -> canonical antigravity promotion once canonical becomes capable: detect fallback marker + capability -> offer/consent (team use re-run / team refresh / upgrade) -> promote that one line; user-chosen bindings untouched.
legacy-fallback-promotion|test-team-legacy-fallback-promotion.sh|pre-0.8.52 UNMARKED deprecated binding (hardened to gemini before provenance markers existed) -> canonical promotion via inference: detect deprecated runtime + differing capable catalog canonical (no marker) -> offer/consent (team use / team refresh / upgrade) -> promote; explicit decline pins (`# sfs-pinned:`) as user intent, non-deprecated overrides never offered.
